(LST2-74: the FizzBuzz example, LANGUAGE.md:3450-3454, verbatim: `but if`
 clauses are checked in order and the FIRST match wins, which is why 15
 prints "FizzBuzz" and not "Fizz" or "Buzz".
 Also covers: LST2-75 (the even/odd example), LST2-78 (clauses checked in
 order), LST2-82 (first match wins), LST2-83 (multiple clauses chain).
